# [[.ID]]

A Heimdall suite written by `bifrost-bench suite init -template [[.Template]]`,
with one complete sample task (`tasks/[[.Sample]]`). The user guide is
`docs/research-tasks.md` in the bench repository.

[[.About]]

## What to edit

1. `tasks/<task>/instruction.md`: the question, as a user would ask it.
2. `tasks/<task>/verifier/tests/research.json`: the hidden spec: how the
   answer is matched (`match`: exact, contains_all, regex or numeric, as the
   answer_match grader does; `abstain: true` when the right answer is "not in
   the sources"), the pages that hold the evidence (`evidence_urls`) and
   whether a pass needs one of them cited (`require_grounding`).
   `corpus_urls.json` beside it lists every page of a fixed corpus; delete it
   for tasks recorded from the live web (then only `evidence_cited` guards
   against invented citations).
3. `cassettes/queries.json` and `cassettes/tavily.cassette.jsonl`: the
   searches and fetches a replay run can answer. A query that was never
   recorded gets an error the agent can read (`external_unmatched` counts
   it). Record them again after changing the queries (see the guide).
4. `tasks/<task>/solution/reference.sh`: the searches a careful agent makes,
   through the websearch tool. Admission runs it in the agent's place, in
   replay mode, and the verifier must pass it.

`controls/` holds what admission requires to fail: the empty control, a
mutant (a wrong answer citing real pages) and an exploit (the right answer
with invented citations, plus fake reward files).

## Layout

```
suite.yaml                          track research, the websearch service, the tavily API
services/websearch/                 the websearch MCP server (Python standard library)
cassettes/                          recorded Tavily calls (replay) and the recording list
probes/model-outage.yaml            gateway fault
probes/search-outage.yaml           every search errors
probes/stale-results.yaml           oldest pages first
probes/hostile-page.yaml            an injected instruction in the first search result
tasks/[[.Sample]]/repo/RESEARCH.md  the house rules the agent follows
tasks/[[.Sample]]/verifier/tests/   hidden verifier, research.json, corpus_urls.json
tasks/[[.Sample]]/solution/         reference control
tasks/[[.Sample]]/controls/         empty, mutant and exploit controls
```

## Check it

```
bifrost-bench suite lint [[.ID]]
bifrost-bench suite lock [[.ID]]
bifrost-bench suite admit [[.ID]]
```

Admission and every run that does not opt in use replay mode: no call
leaves the bench and no Tavily key is needed. A live or record run is
labelled not repeatable and kept off the leaderboard.

## Held-out tasks and canaries

Add `split: held_out` to a task's `task.yaml` to keep it out of `tasks: all`,
out of the public leaderboard and out of what the UI and API serve. To detect
later whether this suite leaked into a model's training data, give it a
contamination canary:

    bifrost-bench suite canary [[.ID]]          # sets canary: <guid> in suite.yaml
    bifrost-bench suite canary -stamp [[.ID]]   # also writes it into every instruction file
    bifrost-bench suite canary-check -text model-output.txt

Stamping changes instruction hashes, so run `suite lock` and `suite admit`
again afterwards; stamp before the first published results, not after. A
canary only catches verbatim copies of stamped text. The bench guide
`docs/held-out-and-canaries.md` has the details.
